<div class="callout">
  <h2>What Professional Chefs Say</h2>
  <p>Professional kitchens have used Thermomix machines for decades, long before the home version became popular. The appeal is the same one home cooks get: precise, repeatable temperature control and the ability to emulsify, purée, and hold a sauce without someone standing over it. Restaurants commonly use one in prep for ultra-smooth purées, silky soups, custards, and stable emulsified sauces that would otherwise tie up a line cook.</p>
  <p>Most professional chefs treat it as a precision prep tool, not a replacement for a stove, grill, or fryer — which mirrors exactly how it fits into a home kitchen. It's a workhorse for the stirred, blended, and gently cooked work; the pan or oven still handles the searing and crisping.</p>
</div>

